const CONCEPTS = [
 ['Rocket vs air-breathing engines','A rocket carries both fuel and oxidizer / reaction mass and can produce thrust in vacuum. Air-breathing jets draw oxidizer from the atmosphere.','Roket dışarıdan oksijene ihtiyaç duymaz; bu yüzden uzayda da çalışır.','Classification'],
 ['Can a rocket travel faster than its exhaust?','Yes. There is no universal constraint u≤u_2. The craft can accumulate velocity while continuously ejecting reaction mass.','Araç hızı egzoz hızını aşabilir; itki prensibi momentum korunumu.','Traps'],
 ['Why does subsonic gas accelerate in a converging duct?','From dA/A=(M²−1)dv/v: when M<1, positive dv requires negative dA.','Subsonic hızlandırma → alan daralmalı.','Nozzle'],
 ['Why does supersonic gas accelerate in a diverging duct?','For M>1, positive dv requires positive dA. It is the opposite of incompressible intuition.','Süpersonik hızlandırma → alan genişlemeli.','Nozzle'],
 ['Meaning of choking','At fixed p1,T1,At and ideal gas conditions, M=1 at the throat and ṁ reaches its maximum; further lowering back pressure does not increase ṁ.','Boğulma akışın durması değildir; kütle debisi maksimuma ulaşmıştır.','Nozzle'],
 ['What is sonic at the throat?','Local velocity equals local speed of sound: v*=a*. The chamber sound speed is different because T1>T*.','Boğazda M=1, hız sıfır değil.','Nozzle'],
 ['What stays constant in isentropic nozzle flow?','Stagnation temperature and pressure stay constant only when adiabatic, no shaft work, and isentropic (no shocks/friction); mass flow stays constant in steady flow.','Şok varsa toplam basınç azalır.','Thermo'],
 ['What falls and what rises along an accelerating ideal nozzle?','Static pressure, density and temperature decrease; flow velocity and Mach number usually increase. T1 remains constant.','Statik u2 toplam (stagnation) büyüklüklerini ayır.','Thermo'],
 ['Why does c* not depend on exit area?','Its ideal expression depends on R, k and T1 (or p0At/ṁ), not A2; it reflects chamber/combustion and gas properties.','c* combustion quality; CF nozzle quality.','Fundamentals'],
 ['Difference between c and c*','c=F/ṁ=I_s g0 includes pressure thrust; c*=p0At/ṁ is characteristic chamber velocity. They are related by c=CF c*.','Bu iki c kesinlikle aynı değil.','Traps'],
 ['Underexpanded nozzle','p_2>p_3. Gas still has excess exit pressure and expands externally in expansion waves; pressure thrust is positive.','Çıkış basıncı dış ortamdan büyükse underexpanded.','Expansion'],
 ['Overexpanded nozzle','p_2<p_3. Ambient pressure compresses the plume; shocks may form, and severe cases can cause separation and side loads.','Dış basınç daha büyük; şok u2 ayrılma riski.','Expansion'],
 ['Ideally expanded nozzle','p_2=p_3. Exit pressure matches surroundings for the design condition. The pressure thrust term is zero.','Basınç itki terimi sıfır ama momentum itkisi devam eder.','Expansion'],
 ['Why does ideal thrust increase in vacuum?','As p3 falls, pressure-thrust term (p2−p3)A2 rises while engine exit conditions are assumed fixed.','Vakumda F=ṁu2+peAe.','Performance'],
 ['Why is a vacuum nozzle often larger?','Low external pressure permits larger expansion area ratio without severe overexpansion and separation; extra expansion can improve exit velocity.','Vakum lülesi daha büyük genleşme oranı kullanabilir.','Expansion'],
 ['Why does a sea-level test of a vacuum engine need care?','Large ε can overexpand at sea level and cause shocks, separation and unsteady asymmetric side forces. Shorter substitute nozzles are sometimes used.','Yüksek irtifa motorunu deniz seviyesinde test etmek risklidir.','Expansion'],
 ['Is separation always symmetric?','Separation may often be approximately axisymmetric in steady operation, but during start-up it may be asymmetric and produce large transverse forces.','Özellikle start-up esnasında yan yükler doğar.','Expansion'],
 ['What happens if chamber area is only near throat area?','Entrance velocity can become significant; acceleration and viscous losses increase. Lecture says chamber area 4× throat is a rough point where chamber gas speed may be neglected.','Ac/At≈4 bilgisi 03 p.22 slaytında yer alıyor.','Geometry'],
 ['Converging-throat geometry sensitivity','A smooth converging and throat contour often has relatively small effect on performance compared with divergence losses, expansion and flow separation.','Hocanın 03 p.23 notu.','Geometry'],
 ['What are real nozzle losses?','Wall friction/boundary layer, divergence of exit velocity, heat loss, nonuniform flow, chemistry changes and shocks reduce delivered performance from ideal.','İdeal model çok sayıda varsayım yapıyor.','Real flow'],
 ['What is frozen-composition flow?','Gas species composition is assumed fixed within the nozzle after upstream chamber equilibrium; real reacting flow may deviate.','Nozzle içinde kimyasal bileşim sabit kabul edilir.','Assumptions'],
 ['How does k affect critical pressure ratio?','p*/p1 = [2/(k+1)]^{k/(k−1)}. For k=1.2 ratio≈0.564, k=1.4≈0.528.','Ezberden önce formülü u2 gamma etkisini bil.','Thermo'],
 ['Why does hotter chamber gas help?','In ideal gas theory, exit velocity grows roughly with √(R T1) at fixed pressure ratio and k; larger T1 helps speed, with material limits.','Egzoz hızı sıcaklığın kareköküyle değişir.','Performance'],
 ['How does molecular weight influence nozzle performance?','R=Ru/MW: lower molecular weight gives higher R and generally higher ideal exhaust velocity and I_s at fixed T1 and k.','Hafif yanma ürünleri yüksek özgül gaz sabiti sağlar.','Performance'],
 ['Why do electric thrusters often have high I_s and low thrust?','For limited jet power, F≈2Pj/u2; increasing u2 reduces thrust while propellant use also falls.','Enerji kısıtı: daha yüksek egzoz hızı, daha küçük momentum debisi.','Performance'],
 ['What does thrust-to-weight mean in Table 2-1?','Ratio of thrust to the FULL propulsion system sea-level weight, including propellants but excluding payload per the lecture table footnote. It is not thrust in newtons.','T/W boyutsuzdur, F [N] ile karıştırma.','Ranges'],
 ['What does I_s in seconds mean?','A performance measure F/(ṁg0), not the duration a rocket operates. High I_s usually implies less propellant needed per unit impulse.','I_s saniye cinsinden olsa bile yanma süresi değildir.','Fundamentals'],
 ['Why does higher exit velocity not imply higher force at fixed jet power?','Pj=½ṁu2², F≈ṁu2 → F≈2Pj/u2. Energy cost increases quadratically with velocity.','Formülü türetip sözlü yorumunu yapabilmelisin.','Fundamentals'],
 ['Difference between impulse and thrust','Thrust is instantaneous rate of momentum transfer (N); total impulse is the integrated thrust–time area (N·s).','Tüm itki eğrisinin alanı total impulse.','Fundamentals'],
 ['What makes dual-level thrust profiles useful?','High initial thrust can rapidly accelerate or launch; reduced later thrust can sustain motion or limit acceleration, g-loads or aerodynamic stress.','Boost u2 sustain aşamaları.','Applications'],
 ['Combustion efficiency vs c-star efficiency','The lecture notes discuss combustion efficiency around 94–99% and characteristic-velocity efficiency around 92–99.5% (typical figures, not universal guaranteed limits). The latter compares delivered to ideal c*.', 'Yüzdeleri u2 verim tanımlarını karıştırma; değerler motora göre değişir.', 'Performance'],
 ['What is characteristic-velocity efficiency?','η_c* = c*delivered / c*ideal, conventionally expressed as a percentage. It assesses real chamber performance relative to thermochemical ideal behavior.', 'c* verimi gerçek/ideal c* oranıdır.', 'Performance'],
 ['Propulsive efficiency as rocket speed increases','With x=u/c, the Sutton ideal definition gives ηp=2x/(1+x²). It reaches 100% at x=1 and decreases again at x>1, while the rocket still produces thrust.', 'u>c olabilir; itki devam eder ancak propulsive efficiency azalır.', 'Fundamentals'],
 ['Engine type: monopropellant','One stored propellant decomposes over a catalyst or through another process (e.g. hydrazine); simplified plumbing compared to bipropellant.', 'Tek akışkan; yakıt u2 oksitleyici ayrı tanklarda değil.', 'Engines'],
 ['Engine type: bipropellant','Fuel and oxidizer are stored separately, fed to an injector and mixed/react in a combustion chamber.','İki tank u2 iki besleme hattı göster.','Engines'],
 ['Engine type: solid rocket motor','Fuel and oxidizer ingredients are already integrated into solid grain; casing, igniter, grain, throat and nozzle are key items.','Basit yapı; itki kontrolü genellikle sınırlı.','Engines'],
 ['Engine type: hybrid motor','Typically solid fuel grain plus separate liquid/gaseous oxidizer feed; port regression changes fuel flow during burn.','Bir katı bir akışkan bileşen.','Engines'],
 ['Engine type: cold gas','Stored pressurized gas expands through a nozzle with no combustion; simple but relatively low exhaust velocity and I_s.','Tabloda cold gas aralığı resimde; Table 2-1 satırı değil.','Engines'],
 ['Engine type: ion/Hall','Electrical energy accelerates ions or plasma; good for long-duration, low-thrust maneuvering, not typical direct surface launch.','Yüksek I_s, düşük T/W.','Engines'],
 ['What is ideal vs delivered performance?','Ideal assumes lossless quasi-1D thermodynamics; delivered includes real combustion, flow and hardware losses. Standard-condition values define measurement reference; guaranteed minimum is contractual bound.','03 p.25 dört performans kategorisini listele.','Real flow'],
 ['What does nozzle alignment/divergence loss mean?','Exhaust momentum not parallel to centerline contributes less axial thrust, approximately reduced by a cosine projection.','Çıkış hızının her bileşeni axial thrust üretmez.','Real flow'],
];
